  "part": {
    "family": "Sony SPC700",
    "role": "the processor inside the SNES audio unit",
    "quotedFrom": "page C-1",
    "quote": "An SPC700 series is used for the SNES sound source CPU. However, standby and sleep modes cannot be used."
  },
  "conditionalBranches": {
    "quotedFrom": "page C-2",
    "quote": "Note: The number of cycles of conditional branching commands are appropriate to cases when there is no branching to the left side and there is branching to the right side.",
    "meaning": "A cycle figure written as two numbers separated by a slash gives the count when the branch is not taken first and when it is taken second."
  },
  "notStated": [
    "What happens inside a cycle. The tables give a count per instruction and no breakdown, so nothing here can settle which address the part drives on which cycle.",
    "Reset state. Appendix C describes the instruction set and says nothing about what the registers hold at power on.",
    "Interrupt timing. The manual gives BRK and RETI as instructions and no figure for an interrupt the part accepts.",
    "The eight bits of the program status word are named in table C-2 and their power-on values are not given."
  ],
